baseboard IO control ASIC for DEC TURBOchannel systems The driver
provides  support for the DEC proprietary IOCTL ASIC found on all
DEC TURBOchannel machines with MIPS (DECstation 5000 series,  ex‐
cluding  the  5000/200)  and  Alpha (3000‐series) processors.  On
these machines (including the 5000/200),  all  baseboard  devices
should  be  configured  as  children of the device.  The provides
hardware DMA channels and interrupt support for several baseboard
devices, including one SCSI  device  with  a  scatter/gather  DMA
channel, an mc146818‐compatible an Am7930 audio device one or two
two‐port serial devices, and a AMD 7990 LANCE Ethernet interface.
The  is  also used for the floppy‐disc drive and audio/ISDN hard‐
ware on the Personal DECstation and  audio‐equipped  TURBOchannel
Alphas,  where the hardware provides a scatter‐gather DMA channel
between the 16‐bit device and the 32‐bit DMA address space.  Sup‐
port for scatter‐gather DMA eliminates the  need  for  additional
copying.   A  baseboard  SCSI  adaptor  attached  to an will give
slightly better performance than  its  counterpart.   The  driver
first appeared in derived from DECstation boot‐time configuration
code  in The DECstation 5000/200 does not actually have an IOASIC
chip, but for consistency it must be configured as if it did.
